<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage back above 7 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage back above 7 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage rose to 7.344 billion rand on Tuesday, the Reserve Bank said.</p>
<p>On Monday the shortage was pegged at 6.743 billion rand -- a six-month low -- although a Reserve Bank official said on Tuesday that the reason for the fall had been a mismatch in government flows and that he expected the shortage to correct over the next couple of days.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
